== B. the opening ==
paragraphs before "The machine": 4
  paragraph 1: 66 words; begins 'Two players meet again and again, in the game call'
  paragraph 2: 99 words; begins 'Which ways of playing survive? I let a hundred sma'
  paragraph 3: 32 words; begins 'I called it the handshake and thought I had found '
  paragraph 4: 19 words; begins 'To see it happen, open the live page (its settings'
old opening, sentence by sentence:
  [1] Two players meet again and again, in the game called the prisoner's dilemma.
  [2] Each time, each can cooperate or cheat (from here on, defect), and cheating pays unless both do it.
  [3] Now and then a move comes out wrong; I call that a slip.
  [4] It is a small picture of a common bind: both sides do well if both cooperate, and each is tempted to cheat.
  [5] Which ways of playing survive?
  [6] I let a hundred small machines, each one a way of playing, breed and mutate to find out, and when a few moves in a hundred slipped, the population kept coming back to the same machine.
  [7] I called it the handshake and thought I had found something.
  [8] Others had found it in 2006, also by evolving machines, and in 2012 it was analysed more thoroughly than I managed.
first new paragraph is old sentences in the order: [1, 2, 4, 3] (None = not word for word an old sentence)
third new paragraph is old sentences: [7, 8]
second new paragraph, sentence by sentence against the old:
    OLD  Which ways of playing survive?
    NEW  I let a hundred small machines, each one a way of playing, breed and mutate to find out, and when a few moves in a hundred slipped, the population kept coming back to the same machine: it defects until the other side has defected twice in a row, and then cooperates for as long as they do.
    NEW  With 2% of moves slipping, 59% of all moves among the hundred machines were cooperative, against 25% with no slips; among a thousand machines the two are close, which is the first thing I got wrong (below).
the old sentence "I let a hundred..." less its full stop is the start of the new one: True ; what was added: ': it defects until the other side has defected twice in a row, and then cooperates for as long as they do.'

